obuchar pairs a high-single-digit polling average with a massive money advantage in a state leaning Democratic, and prediction markets price her win odds in the low-to-mid 90s alongside Likely-to-Solid ratings from every major rater. The main caveat is September's tightening, led by a Republican-sponsored poll showing just a two-point gap, which argues for staying below the safest tier.", "watch": "Whether the $10 million Demuth-aligned PAC infusion and GOP airtime sustain the late tightening through the still-unscheduled debates and early voting.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tim Walz's retirement leaves Minnesota's governorship open, and Senator Amy Klobuchar enters as the clear favorite against Republican Lisa Demuth. Polling through mid-September shows Klobuchar ahead by anywhere from two to fifteen points, with the latest surveys narrowing to single digits after wider summer margins. She has vastly out-raised Demuth, though a Demuth-aligned committee recently received a $10 million infusion and Republican donors are funding airtime.\n\nRaters across the spectrum place the race between Likely and Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price a Democratic win around 94%. Minnesota's Democratic lean and a favorable environment support the edge. The campaign has stayed largely cordial, with healthcare a recurring point of clash, but outside spending is climbing and the candidates have yet to agree on debate logistics.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}]}